{"wrong":"is so bad recently","fix":"has been so bad recently","why":"Use present perfect for a recent situation continuing into the present."}
{"wrong":"everyday","fix":"every day","why":"'Everyday' is an adjective; 'every day' means each day."}
{"wrong":"have no mood","fix":"am not in the mood","why":"Use 'be in the mood' to express willingness or desire."}
